# The conforming hand (#385.7) on the glove of the classic arm (#466.2, `arms classic-hand glove`): the runtime is
# asked for the controller-conforming joints (SteamVR's own fist around the Index handle,
# XR_EXT_hand_joints_motion_range), the glove is driven by the joints' orientations, and a held weapon closes the hand
# to a hilt pose sized by the hilt. The palm behind the grip (palmToGrip 2.5 - 4.5) was the custom glove's own
# placement on the handle (#486): the glove at the Arx wrist sits where the Arx hand does.
# PROPOSED status.json keys (385.7 implements them):
#   vr.hands.<hand>.motionRange = conforming | unobstructed | none
#   vr.hands.<hand>.hiltPose = default | captured | live | none      (none: no weapon in that hand)
# The simulated runtime reports XR_EXT_hand_joints_motion_range and fills the conforming joints.
# The right hand holds the sword (mvp-items); `grip capture` stores the current conforming pose as the hilt pose.
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 hand-conforming
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence hand-conforming -Save mvp-items
@sim idle
@save mvp-items
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
arms classic
arms classic-hand glove
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.active eq true
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@assert vr.body.left.posed eq true
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq classic
@assert vr.body.right.custom.gloveDrawn eq true

# The conforming range is the one in use on both hands
@assert vr.hands.left.active eq true
@assert vr.hands.right.active eq true
@assert vr.hands.left.motionRange eq conforming
@assert vr.hands.right.motionRange eq conforming

# The sword in the right hand: a hilt pose is in use, whatever its origin; the left hand holds nothing
@assert vr.body.right.fingers.holds eq true
@assert vr.hands.right.hiltPose ne none
@assert vr.hands.left.hiltPose eq none

# Capturing the current conforming pose succeeds and the hilt pose is the captured one from then on
grip capture
@frames 15
@assert vr.hands.right.hiltPose eq captured

# The held rule is unchanged: the tracked fingers say open, the hand stays on the hilt
vr-sim hand right fingers 0 0 0
@frames 30
@assert vr.body.right.fingers.source eq held
@assert vr.hands.right.hiltPose ne none

# The hand before the face: the closed hand on the hilt (judged on the capture)
vr-sim hand right pos 0.12 -0.1 -0.35
vr-sim hand right rot 0 90 0
vr-sim head rot 0 -15 0
@frames 20
@assert vr.body.right.error lt 1
@shot hand-conforming

@assert errors eq 0
